In `app/assets/javascripts/discourse/models/store.js.es6`, plural hydration was added:
```js
const hydrated = obj[k].map(function(id) {
  return self._lookupSubType(subType, type, id, root);
});
obj[self.pluralize(subType)] = hydrated || [];
```
Because `map(...)` always returns an array, `hydrated || []` will never replace it. If `_lookupSubType(...)` returns `false`/`undefined` for an id that is not present in the side-loaded `root`, that falsy value will remain in the hydrated array (i.e., “leaking” false entries).

The updated JS tests (`test/javascripts/models/store-test.js.es6`) only ass

